#: <RELIC_ROOT>/docs/source/public/theory/index.rst:4
msgid "The Recomposable Ecosystem Library for Integrated Coupling (RELIC) formulates terrestrial and interfacial Earth-system simulation as a composable graph of typed PyTorch ``FunctorBase`` operators acting on governed state reservoirs. Universal mass, energy, and entropy balance laws are separated from discrete cochain and port-Hamiltonian operators, numerical time integrators, and sphere-specific constitutive closures (*Methods of Ecological Analysis*, Chapters 1--30)."
msgstr "可重组生态系统集成耦合库（Recomposable Ecosystem Library for Integrated Coupling, RELIC）将陆地及界面地球系统模拟表述为作用于受控状态储库之上的类型化 PyTorch ``FunctorBase`` 算子可组合计算图。普适的质量、能量与熵平衡定律同离散上链及端口哈密顿算子、数值时间积分器以及各圈层特异的本构闭合相分离（书稿《生态学分析方法》第 1--30 章）。"

#: <RELIC_ROOT>/docs/source/public/theory/index.rst:12
msgid "Equations across these pages define the live ``forward()`` and ``StateManager`` contracts of the installed RELIC package. Literature constitutive forms are distinguished from canonical runtime operators: structural and thermodynamic equivalence claims (`Level 0` through `Level 5`) are owned exclusively by each process's declarative ``IPHSEquivalenceCertificate``."
msgstr "本部分各页面的方程定义了已安装 RELIC 软件包中现行 ``forward()`` 与 ``StateManager`` 的运行时契约。文献中的本构形式与规范运行时算子严格区分：结构与热力学等价性声明（ `Level 0` 至 `Level 5` ）由各过程的声明式 ``IPHSEquivalenceCertificate`` 唯一持有。"

